A||N||6||chris6878||dash lights stopped working.........||||5||
Z||000000||chris6878||01-12-2000||12:35 AM||||My interior dash lights stopped working.. the ones that light up your gauges and so on...     i checked the fuse..   It was shot...   replaced with a new fuse... and the dang lights still wont work.... they worked fine before though...?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||01-12-2000||04:20 AM||||If the rest of your dash lights (HVAC controls, etc) don't work either, check the dimmer knob.  Could be either turned down by mistake or bad.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bill Osmer||01-12-2000||10:08 AM||||Or the power transistor module (see previous threads covering this)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||01-12-2000||10:20 AM||||Under the drivers side of the dash, you will find a heat sink, with a metal diamond-shaped device (transistor) mounted in the middle. (The transistor is actually what controls the dash lights. The dimmer knob only controls the transistor.) On the back side of the transistor there are two prongs that go through the heat sink and plug in to sockets behind the heatsink. What usually happens is that the contacts will get sprung, or oxidized, and won't grip the pins. The most permanent way to fix this is to put a dab of solder on the connections. If you remove the transistor from the heatsink (not necessary), you will notice white paste all over everything. This is thermal compound. It's supposed to be there. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||dogtired||01-12-2000||12:17 PM||||I know this sounds like a crock?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>But check your tail light fuse!<BR>If its out no dash lights  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>Just something else to check?||||reg||6
Z||000005||wwh0001||01-11-2000||01:35 PM||||I would check the heat sink referred to earlier. Both my 88 and 87 had the same problem. When I cleaned the prongs on the transitor they worked again. Easy to get to an easy to fix. Located under dash on drivers side just to the right of the steering column.||||reg||1
Z||000006||chris6878||01-11-2000||01:54 PM||||I  will look into this in the morning...  thanks for the replies...<P>chris||||reg||14
